  "assumptions": [
    "SIFMA is the sole calendar provider. Its U.S. recommendations apply to trading in the fixed-income products identified by SIFMA and are recommendations subject to change, not universal loan-contract terms.",
    "A published SIFMA full-close recommendation makes the date non-business for this screening calendar. A published early close remains a business day and is retained as an event; SIFMA states that early closes do not affect settlement closing time.",
    "Weekends are deterministic for every supported year. Weekday dates outside the maintained published range remain unknown; current holiday patterns are neither backcast nor projected.",
    "The governing agreement must establish whether this SIFMA market calendar applies to a loan date. The engine flags dates for review and never adjusts source values."
